A||||16||Heretic||Best Win / Most Embarassing Defeat......||||12||
Z||000000||Heretic||08-16-2001||07:19 PM||||What is your best win and most embarassing defeat in your Fiero. Unfortunately , i cant answer this question just yet... a few more years.||||reg||12
Z||000001||FieroLisa||08-16-2001||07:44 PM||||I was trying to be a harda$$ in my 2.5 coupe and I lined up with a hearse at a light, some old fat guy and his daughter.... guess who won.  THE HEARSE. talk about embarassing. Those 92 horsies were just not on my side that day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||08-16-2001||08:22 PM||||My best win was vs a C-5 Vette convertable going through fairly sharp corners at 115+mph  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The vette might be a better car, but I was the better, or more crazy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> , driver that day. <P>Hmm, most embarassing loss......well I've gotten my doors completely blown off by a 2000 T/A on the freeway.  He was putting buslengths on me in a matter of seconds.  but that was expected, but it was still pretty embarassing.<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||08-16-2001||08:37 PM||||The only 2 defeats so far was against a Jag S-type, and a heavily modded gen-II MR-2. Wasn't embarrassing in the least. I was laughing! I had the jump on both of them, but got passed justly right after. <BR>Best win? 2 of 'em. Riced out Accord-4door, loaded with Southdale punks, and even more loaded with badly mounted fibreglass. Not even close. They had the start when they squeeled the tires. Then it was rear-view-waving. 2-3 car-lengths by 70kph. They turned off. Second, was a pair of punks in a riced out Sunfire GT. Even their chrome tips couldn't save 'em. about 3/4 car length at ~70kph. Then the blow-by when I let off. Of course. ||||reg||10
Z||000004||NOS3800||08-16-2001||11:37 PM||||Best Kill- At track, I pulled a Street legal pro stock looking 5.0 Mustang. You know fat tires and slammed. Well he proceeds to do a big long professional style burnout, I was impressed, really... I just drove around the water box(no need to do burnout cause I have no traction problems). We stage, light turns green and WHAM I pull two carlengths right from the light and increase it to three buy the time we cross the finish line. He ran a 13.9 to my 13.5. Best thing is I got it on tape!<BR>Worse was at nite on a four lane road, I was on my way home from my gf house. Suddenly( like out of nowhere) there is a 2nd generation riced Supra(the real long type) next to me reving his motor at 40 mph. I didn't have my NOS bottle open, and we were going 40mph which is a bad spot for my 3800, no power and the tranny doesn't downshift. But I was thinking, he revs again and I say its go time!!!! I floor it and DAMN, no downshift!! He's gone by the time I manually put the trans in 2nd! It was amazing how fast he was! All I heard was SWOOOOOOOSH!!! To make things worse, my brother was in the car with me. After 5 minutes of silence, he says" You know, I coulda taken him in my SC3800 Fiero". You know what?....., Just SHUTUP!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||6
Z||000005||banditbalz||08-16-2001||11:50 PM||||Best Win / Most Embarassing Defeat...... <BR>Best was like 3 years ago when I took a close friend of mine's 91 Mustang GT. He had a 5 speed 5.0L with Flowmaster exhaust, and a cold air setup, the rest was stock. We both had girlfriends with us as I embarassed him from one set of lights to the next. I was feeling a little confident of my stock,  4 speed 2.8, so we took it out to Cayuga Dragway Park. Again, I beat him through the quarter mile three times in a row before he decided he didn't want to abuse his Stang anymore!<BR>Most embarassing was this spring when Becky (my fiance) and I were out cruising and came upon 2 kids in a new silver C5 Vette. After carefully scanning the horizon for boxes of kittens, we decided it was a go. Man, I love these cars. By the time I hit 3rd, the vette was like 5 car lengths on me. Embarassed? not really considering we were side by side through most of second gear and he had a 200hp advantage...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Becker_1.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||08-16-2001||11:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>I was trying to be a harda$$ in my 2.5 coupe and I lined up with a hearse at a light, some old fat guy and his daughter.... guess who won.  THE HEARSE. talk about embarassing. Those 92 horsies were just not on my side that day   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That really shouldn't be embarassing, Lisa.  Especially if it was and old Cadillac Hearse, say around 69-73.  They had Limousine packages or Ambulance packages in them and had 472 - 500 cubic inches and almost 400HP!  Even late model Hearses have the heavy duty drivetrain (whatever was available that year).<P>You want something FAST, a late 60's to early 70's Cadillac Limo with the "Coachman" package.  It had a special "Coachman" engine in it.  Designed for diplomats, etc. that might need to get gone in a hurry.  That's the kind of limo the President would use.  You need LOTS of power to pull an armoured limo.  Put that engine in a regular Caddy or even a non-armoured limo, and you've got one fast sumb!tch!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Boomtastic||08-16-2001||11:54 PM||||Best win(s) - <BR>a) Racing a friend in his 300ZX (non-turbo) down the highway. Neither could get by the other, and since I had him off the line I kept my lead until we came into a rotary. His handling out performed mine, and I had to back off. (I've actually spun the car on that rotary, so I was also a bit gunshy ..)  <P>b) Racing another Formula from RI into MA on Rt 195. We were hitting triple digit speeds, him on my tail when he could be, when we passed an older Porsche on the right. All of a sudden I hear engine whine, and I look over and the guy in the Porsche had downshifted and was going for it! The hood of his car lurched up, but he didn't have the oomph to pull him past.<P>c) Racing a BMW on Rt 95 North in RI. 20 Exits of him trying to pass me. He never had a chance.<P>Worst Loss -<BR>a) Blew the motor in the Formula at 125 mph racing a Volvo turbo sedan. 2 phone calls to the State Police, a 2 hour wait, and the next day off of work to fetch the car home via tow dolly. That hurt!<P>b) Lost a race to a Plymouth Horizon. I thought the guy was kidding when I pulled behind him and saw he had a roll cage in the car. He walked away from me! I later found out that he had blown mad money on the motor and turbo unit, thus giving him over 300 hp. Every winter he has to tear down the motor. I met him at the shop where he was doing the tear down and grilled him about the race. He didn't remember it.<P><P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||08-17-2001||03:54 AM||||Haven't had too many races with the quad yet... toasted a few riceboys and whatnot, and absolutly walked all over an 80's firebird with some custom sidepipes on the freeway..<P>First real loss would have to be from tonight.. passed a very nice C3 corvette that was stuck behind a slower car.  The road we were on goes from 35mph to 50mph, and I gave it a bit of gas as I passed him.  Stayed at 50 and sure enough, he zooms along next to me.  Downshifted to second and it was on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  By the time we hit 80 he had only pulled about a half carlength, though.  I did have a friend with me so that was some extra weight to slow me down a little, but I'm not making excuses  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000009||firstfiero||08-17-2001||09:09 AM||||       Beat a kid not long ago in a new civic si. He has a show car with alot of cash outside and under the hood. Raced him block to block three times and lit his candle every damn time. He was MAD,MAD,MAD. He was to dumb to realize that in block to block races he doesn't have the torque to keep up with my girl!<BR>       Haven't had an imbarasing one. I usually know when I'm going to lose to someone.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000010||rogergarrison||08-17-2001||10:50 AM||||I got totally smoked by a new vette on I-270 one of the W09 or whatever there called. felt like i was in a civic.<P>not really a race but fun-im cruising along like 70 and this guy and gf comes flying past in a Hyundai Elantra Im sure going over 100 weaving in and out of traffic. when It was clear and he was just barely in view ahead i stomped it, caught him, passed him so fast I didnt even see his face. slowed back down and he did too never to catch back up.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fiero5||08-17-2001||02:36 PM||||I have had a bunch of cool wins in a variety of my Fieros.<BR>The best kills would easily have to be in my Fiero1, a white 84SE 4 speed tweeked by my Dad just a "teeny" bit.<BR>I remember one off hand against a modded late model (say 89-90) Mustang GT.<BR>I pull up to a set of lights and next to me is this nice Mustang GT. Hood scoop, black paint with an engine rumbling like a beefed up monster. The guy looks over at my quieter running decaled Fiero and smiles. We are at the lights next to the McDonalds on Rt. 12-A. Anyway, were side by side and he's just reving the crap out of his engine waiting for the light to change. Light hits green and were off. Luckily I had my engine reved a bit so when I  popped the clutch, I snapped forward with a good take off. I got the better jump off the line and quickly reved up and shifted to second, then quickly to third. It's about a quarter mile stretch to the end where it turns from two lanes to one, just past Freindly's on the right. I was in the right lane which is the lane that has to merge to the left when it ends. I beat him to the merge by a car length or so.<BR>Smiling in victory I then shifted to fourth and let it coast down to 45mph. I never did look down to see how fast we are going. My speedo only reads to 85mph, so when I am taking on someone, it usually doesn't do any good to chance taking my eyes off the road for a second anyway, as it's always pegged anyway.<BR>I had a good one in Fiero5 against a Trans-Am too. I could tell he was ambarrassed when I smoked him going from exit 18 to exit 20 on I-89. He knew the car too, as we both had them at a local cruise meet one night before that, so he knew it was "just" a 4 banger. The next cruise meet a few weeks later, i was a couple rows over looking at some older Mustangs or something, and I catch him quickly peeking into my engine area looking at it a bit closer. Wish I had a camera on me then.<BR>Fiero9, my red 86SS looks meaner than it is, but it is still darn quick off the line, even for an automatic. I have taken tons of other sports cars thru the lights many times with it. I have more fun doing that kind of thing with my manual Fieros though, than with the automatics. Marians 88 is an automatic, and that thing is really quick off the line. That engine is so strong! Still can't catch Fiero1 though, heh, heh.<P>Worse that I can remember quickly would be in my Gold 86 Fiero4 coming back from New York. I was blasting up the highway and spotted a Z-28 hot dogging it onto an on ramp. He spots me as he enters onto the highway and picks up speed to catch me. Fiero4 is a 5 speed, so I down shift to fourth to pick up speed quick, then back to fifth to get some top end speed under me. The early model Z-28 Camaro is still catching up to me with no sign of me pulling away at all as our speed is still climbing. I felt like I was driving through a foot of water as he went by me so easily. The other times when I got beat in Fiero4, I was at least able to give them a run for their money for a bit first. Not that time.<P>Steve||||reg||12
Z||000012||Fiero5||08-17-2001||03:07 PM||||I have had a bunch of cool wins in a variety of my Fieros.<BR>The best kills would easily have to be in my Fiero1, a white 84SE 4 speed tweeked by my Dad just a "teeny" bit.<BR>I remember one off hand against a modded late model (say 89-90) Mustang GT.<BR>I pull up to a set of lights and next to me is this nice Mustang GT. Hood scoop, black paint with an engine rumbling like a beefed up monster. The guy looks over at my quieter running decaled Fiero and smiles. We are at the lights next to the McDonalds on Rt. 12-A. Anyway, were side by side and he's just reving the crap out of his engine waiting for the light to change. Light hits green and were off. Luckily I had my engine reved a bit so when I  popped the clutch, I snapped forward with a good take off. I got the better jump off the line and quickly reved up and shifted to second, then quickly to third. It's about a quarter mile stretch to the end where it turns from two lanes to one, just past Freindly's on the right. I was in the right lane which is the lane that has to merge to the left when it ends. I beat him to the merge by a car length or so.<BR>Smiling in victory I then shifted to fourth and let it coast down to 45mph. I never did look down to see how fast we are going. My speedo only reads to 85mph, so when I am taking on someone, it usually doesn't do any good to chance taking my eyes off the road for a second anyway, as it's always pegged anyway.<BR>I had a good one in Fiero5 against a Trans-Am too. I could tell he was ambarrassed when I smoked him going from exit 18 to exit 20 on I-89. He knew the car too, as we both had them at a local cruise meet one night before that, so he knew it was "just" a 4 banger. The next cruise meet a few weeks later, i was a couple rows over looking at some older Mustangs or something, and I catch him quickly peeking into my engine area looking at it a bit closer. Wish I had a camera on me then.<BR>Fiero9, my red 86SS looks meaner than it is, but it is still darn quick off the line, even for an automatic. I have taken tons of other sports cars thru the lights many times with it. I have more fun doing that kind of thing with my manual Fieros though, than with the automatics. Marians 88 is an automatic, and that thing is really quick off the line. That engine is so strong! Still can't catch Fiero1 though, heh, heh.<P>Worse that I can remember quickly would be in my Gold 86 Fiero4 coming back from New York. I was blasting up the highway and spotted a Z-28 hot dogging it onto an on ramp. He spots me as he enters onto the highway and picks up speed to catch me. Fiero4 is a 5 speed, so I down shift to fourth to pick up speed quick, then back to fifth to get some top end speed under me. The early model Z-28 Camaro is still catching up to me with no sign of me pulling away at all as our speed is still climbing. I felt like I was driving through a foot of water as he went by me so easily. The other times when I got beat in Fiero4, I was at least able to give them a run for their money for a bit first. Not that time.<P>Steve||||reg||12
Z||000013||Fiero5||08-17-2001||03:10 PM||||Oh crap! How do I delete/edit one of those back off?<P>Steve||||reg||8
Z||000014||rogergarrison||08-17-2001||04:58 PM||||just click on 'edit' icon and backspace it all off. thats how i do it anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000015||88formula||08-17-2001||05:05 PM|||| My 88 formula was to slow to win against any real sports cars in a straight line when it was stock. I had a guy in a Porsche leave me like I was standing still. I did however take a late model Camaro in a short corner.<P>I haven't raced anyone really with the new 3.4 but I did do a 0-50mph sprint with V6 Golf and pretty much left him in the dust, he started it!<P>A friend of mine who has a 350 v8 in his car told me this story. There was a kid in an all wheel drive turbo Eclipse tailgating and revving his engine at my friend’s car. They cane to a stoplight and my friend looked over and said “you looking for a race”. The guy in the Eclipse said, “I’ll destroy that POS.”. The light turned green and they were off. He said when he went into second gear he pulled away from that eclipse all too easily and pretty much embarrassed him. When they got to the next light the confused Eclipse owner who thought it was a 2.8 v6 fiero asked “what the hell do you have in that thing, a 2.8”? My friend looked over and said “just a Chevy 350 v8”. The Eclipse owner drove off at normal speeds probably with a new respect for the fiero. <BR> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fiero5||08-17-2001||05:50 PM||||Well, I tried to delete one of them and it said only Forum leaders can delete. So I tried to edit it by clearing the text out and it keeps saying that I didn't fill in all the required fields. I put in my user name and password, what else is there?<P>Cliff? Help!!!<P>Steve||||reg||5
